><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250509085305+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250509085314+10'00'" name="acb366a5-9f4c-4b83-b44f-b59616ca93e8" page="4" coords="90.953903,345.892426,135.474838,345.892426,90.953903,335.945862,135.474838,335.945862,90.986206,324.875366,330.576111,324.875366,90.986206,315.016479,330.576111,315.016479,79.030991,314.414612,330.575745,314.414551,79.030991,304.555725,330.575745,304.555664,79.031357,303.953796,330.576050,303.953735,79.031357,294.094910,330.576050,294.094879,79.031174,293.492981,330.576416,293.493042,79.031174,283.634125,330.576416,283.634186,79.031296,283.032288,330.575592,283.032227,79.031296,273.173431,330.575592,273.173370,79.031311,272.571472,330.575928,272.571472,79.031311,262.712616,330.575928,262.712585,79.031586,262.110718,330.575592,262.110657,79.031586,252.251831,330.575592,252.251770,79.031326,251.649887,330.575958,251.649948,79.031326,241.791016,330.575958,241.791077,79.031540,241.189194,330.575684,241.189163,79.031540,231.330322,330.575684,231.330292,79.031433,230.728409,316.178497,230.728439,79.031433,220.869537,316.178497,220.869568" rect="78.722900,220.561447,330.884521,346.203247" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Hip/groin ‘discomfort/pain’ were reported by nearly half of thepre-elite U20s basketball players included in this study. Of the play-ers who self-reported discomfort/pain, almost half did not perceivethis to be a problem, likely due to the fact that they reported notraining/playing time loss. Those who self-reported hip/groin painscored lower on five of the six HAGOS subscales (Symptoms; Pain;Function in daily living; Function in sport and recreation; and hipand/or groin Quality of Life), indicating these late-adolescent bas-ketball players perceive hip/groin pain negatively impacts on theirperformance of sporting tasks and also affects their daily lives.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="637.179993,253.892426,821.179993,345.892426"
/></highlight
